msgid "Shared library support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:505
msgid "**EXPERIMENTAL**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:507
msgid ""
"The basic CFI mode described above assumes that the application is a "
"monolithic binary; at least that all possible virtual/indirect call targets "
"and the entire class hierarchy are known at link time. The cross-DSO mode, "
"enabled with **-f[no-]sanitize-cfi-cross-dso** relaxes this requirement by "
"allowing virtual and indirect calls to cross the DSO boundary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:514
msgid ""
"Assuming the following setup: the binary consists of several instrumented "
"and several uninstrumented DSOs. Some of them may be dlopen-ed/dlclose-d "
"periodically, even frequently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:518
msgid "Calls made from uninstrumented DSOs are not checked and just work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:519
msgid "Calls inside any instrumented DSO are fully protected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:520
msgid ""
"Calls between different instrumented DSOs are also protected, with a "
"performance penalty (in addition to the monolithic CFI overhead)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:522
msgid ""
"Calls from an instrumented DSO to an uninstrumented one are unchecked and "
"just work, with performance penalty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ControlFlowIntegrityDesign.md:524
msgid ""
"Calls from an instrumented DSO outside of any known DSO are detected as CFI "
"violations."
msgstr ""

